---
description: Colour contrast — dark text on light surfaces, light text on dark
alwaysApply: true
---

# Contrast rule

- **Light / bright backgrounds** (including solid `--yellow` `#ffd700`): use dark text via `--ink-on-yellow`. Never put light-grey / `--ink-soft` / dark-theme `--ink` on yellow.
- **Dark backgrounds** (page `--bg`, dark `--yellow-wash`): use light text (`--ink` in dark theme, or `--ink-on-yellow-wash` on wash).
- Solid yellow accents stay bright in both themes — always pair with `--ink-on-yellow`, not theme `--ink`.
- Soft wash (`--yellow-wash`) follows the theme — pair with `--ink-on-yellow-wash` (dark brown in light, gold in dark).
